# Autonomous Mission Execution

**Phase 3–5.** Active only after the user locks scope (e.g. "Approved. Scope is locked.").

The approved plan is the contract.

## Execution

- Complete all tasks in order.
- No permission prompts between tasks; no artificial checkpoints after each task.
- Progress: **one line per completed task** during execution.
- Continue through implementation, smallest relevant verification, repairs, commits (when approved), and final gates.

## Allowed without re-asking

- Read project files; edit in-scope files
- Update tests required by the change (new test **files** need explicit user approval)
- Run local verification (`pytest`, lint, build, e2e when in scope)
- Fix failures caused by the current change
- Commits on the active feature branch when the user or approved plan explicitly allows commits
- Docs/checklists required by the approved plan

## Not allowed without explicit approval

- Delete user data or perform unapproved destructive file operations
- Rewrite unrelated architecture or broad refactors outside scope
- Alter secrets, `.env`, or generated artifacts outside scope
- Force push; push/merge to protected branches when checks fail
- Production schema or external service changes beyond the plan

## Final gate (Phase 4)

Run agreed verification from the locked plan (pytest, lint, build, e2e as scoped).

## Merge / PR (Phase 5)

When the mission includes finish work, follow branch-finish rule from the `00-core` index.

Autonomous merge/PR is allowed when checks pass and policy allows. **Stop and report** when: branch protection blocks merge, CI fails, conflicts need human resolution, force push required, or secrets/env changes are needed.

## Completion summary

Changed files, verification commands + results, commit/PR/merge status, skipped checks + reason, remaining risks or exact blocker.
